t. Their\n2644 |         dimensions are given by *width* and *height*. The horizontal baseline\n2645 |         is *left* (default 0).\n2646 | \n2647 |         Many parameters can take either a single value applying to all bars\n2648 |         or a sequence of values, one for each bar.\n2649 | \n2650 |         Parameters\n2651 |         ----------\n2652 |         y : float or array-like\n2653 |             The y coordinates of the bars. See also *align* for the\n2654 |             alignment of the bars to the coordinates.\n2655 | \n2656 |         width : float or array-like\n2657 |             The width(s) of the bars.\n2658 | \n2659 |             Note that if *left* has units (e.g. datetime), *width* should be in\n2660 |             units that are a difference from the value of *left* (e.g. timedelta).\n2661 | \n2662 |         height : float or array-like, default: 0.8\n2663 |             The heights of the bars.\n2664 | \n2665 |             Note that if *y* has units (e.g. datetime), then *height* should be in\n2666 |             units that are a difference (e.g. timedelta) around the *y* values.\n2667 | \n2668 |         left : float or array-like, default: 0\n2669 |             The x coordinates of the left side(s) of the bars.\n2670 | \n2671 |             Note that if *left* has units, then the x-axis will get a Locator and\n2672 |             Formatter appropriate for the units (e.g. dates, or categorical).\n2673 | \n2674 |         align : {'center', 'edge'}, default: 'center'\n2675 |             Alignment of the base to the *y* coordinates*:\n2676 | \n2677 |             - 'center': Center the bars on the *y* positions.\n2678 |             - 'edge': Align the bottom edges of the bars with the *y*\n2679 |               positions.\n2680 | \n2681 |             To align the bars on the top edge pass a negative *height* and\n2682 |             ``align='edge'``.\n2683 | \n2684 |         Returns\n2685 |         -------\n2686 |         `.BarContainer`\n2687 |           