func is a tuple,\n500 |     interpret the first element of the tuple as a function and pass the obj to\n501 |     that function as a keyword argument whose key is the value of the second\n502 |     element of the tuple.\n503 | \n504 |     Parameters\n505 |     ----------\n506 |     func : callable or tuple of (callable, str)\n507 |         Function to apply to this object or, alternatively, a\n508 |         ``(callable, data_keyword)`` tuple where ``data_keyword`` is a\n509 |         string indicating the keyword of ``callable`` that expects the\n510 |         object.\n511 |     *args : iterable, optional\n512 |         Positional arguments passed into ``func``.\n513 |     **kwargs : dict, optional\n514 |         A dictionary of keyword arguments passed into ``func``.\n515 | \n516 |     Returns\n517 |     -------\n518 |     object : the return type of ``func``.\n519 |     \"\"\"\n520 |     if isinstance(func, tuple):\n521 |         # Assigning to func_ so pyright understands that it's a callable\n522 |         func_, target = func\n523 |         if target in kwargs:\n524 |             msg = f\"{target} is both the pipe target and a keyword argument\"\n525 |             raise ValueError(msg)\n526 |         kwargs[target] = obj\n527 |         return func_(*args, **kwargs)\n528 |     else:\n529 |         return func(obj, *args, **kwargs)\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"typing\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound class `pandas/io/parsers/c_parser_wrapper.py:CParserWrapper`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\nJust show the structure of this class due to response length limitations:\n```\nclass CParserWrapper(ParserBase):\n    low_memory: bool\n    _reader: parsers.TextReader\n\n    def __init__(self, src: ReadCsvBuffer[str], **kwds) -> None:\n...\n    def close(self) -> None:\n...\n    def _set_noconvert_columns(self) -> None:\n...\n    def read(\n        self,\n        nrows: int | None = None,\n    ) -> tuple[\n        Index | MultiIndex | None