- [list, list, ...]: Return ([list, list, ...], 'list')\n287 |     - [list, Index, ...]: Return _sanitize_and_check([Index, Index, ...])\n288 |         Lists are sorted and converted to Index.\n289 |     - [Index, Index, ...]: Return ([Index, Index, ...], TYPE)\n290 |         TYPE = 'special' if at least one special type, 'array' otherwise.\n291 | \n292 |     Parameters\n293 |     ----------\n294 |     indexes : list of Index or list objects\n295 | \n296 |     Returns\n297 |     -------\n298 |     sanitized_indexes : list of Index or list objects\n299 |     type : {'list', 'array', 'special'}\n300 |     \"\"\"\n301 |     kinds = {type(index) for index in indexes}\n302 | \n303 |     if list in kinds:\n304 |         if len(kinds) > 1:\n305 |             indexes = [\n306 |                 Index(list(x)) if not isinstance(x, Index) else x for x in indexes\n307 |             ]\n308 |             kinds -= {list}\n309 |         else:\n310 |             return indexes, \"list\"\n311 | \n312 |     if len(kinds) > 1 or Index not in kinds:\n313 |         return indexes, \"special\"\n314 |     else:\n315 |         return indexes, \"array\"\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/core/arrays/arrow/accessors.py:ListAccessor._is_valid_pyarrow_dtype`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n79 | def _is_valid_pyarrow_dtype(self, pyarrow_dtype) -> bool:\n80 |         return (\n81 |             pa.types.is_list(pyarrow_dtype)\n82 |             or pa.types.is_fixed_size_list(pyarrow_dtype)\n83 |             or pa.types.is_large_list(pyarrow_dtype)\n84 |         )\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"typing.List\", \"typing.Tuple\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `pandas/core/dtypes/base.py:ExtensionDtype.type`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n163 | def type(self) -> type_t[Any]:\n164 |         \"\"\"\n165 |         The scalar type for the array, e.g. ``int``\n166 | \n167 |         It's expected ``ExtensionArray[item]`` returns an ins